WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
Start on the day five check, not the original repair.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.940
There are two numbers here.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.500
Match the original ticket, the equipment, and the symptom before you touch an outcome.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.100
Read the repair history.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.690
For this microphone, the cable was replaced because moving it interrupted the audio.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:19.630
Test that condition on the same unit according to your studio procedure.

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.160
Silence from the reporter is not a test.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.540
If you cannot verify the result, leave the check open and arrange a test.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.320
Here the sound cuts out again.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.930
Choose Fault returned.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:36.430
In the note, identify mic five, describe the movement that triggered the dropout, and say what you observed.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.080
Check the number on Reopen before confirming.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.390
Follow Open back to the original and verify its number and reopened state.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.960
Keep the evidence on that repair rather than creating another ticket.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.660
Now compare a separate check for bike twelve.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.480
The reported symptom was a click during climbs.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:57.780
Once the same bike has been tested and the symptom has not returned, select No recurrence.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.670
Look for the saved outcome, open the original, and read the schedule.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:06.550
A pass applies to this check; it is not evidence that a later check has already been done.
